            <ArticleTitle>Enteric duplication cyst of the pancreas: CT findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>105-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Enteric duplication cysts are rare congenital anomalies of the GI tract. We present a most unusual case presenting as a cystic lesion on the pancreas simulating a cystic pancreatic neoplasm. The differential diagnosis of cystic pancreatic lesions as well as duplication cysts is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
